#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529488 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7784e390-875b-5d46-ab94-2c5cda01d4fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529483} {:answer/id #uuid "9439aba3-1d39-5a23-9a1b-53fd1ddca6be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529489} {:answer/id #uuid "d6880dc8-8ad8-519d-a693-57299b6be5e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529496} {:answer/id #uuid "da9cdc3a-cda2-571d-8bc0-e4d740e6cfcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529498} {:answer/id #uuid "daddb35c-2db8-5467-b683-5e18c079dc13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6880dc8-8ad8-519d-a693-57299b6be5e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529496} :answer-field/id #uuid "b496728c-0c7d-5d4b-8ceb-439f00dd77cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529493}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d541dba-0895-564d-b1f6-b95dbb99a330" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=- 2 x - 3 y,$ where $x=3 s - t$ and $y=- s - 2 t.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/21/21cec766fe72965697304ef4288ffb2b090ddfca179210165dbcfd42ec490b27.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y=y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=-2,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =-2, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =3, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s} \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (3)+(-3)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =(-6)+(3) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529494 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a5aca8d-e4a3-529a-930a-8ba48fc7c160" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529478} {:answer/id #uuid "6752aa28-44c5-533c-bfdd-e974e3a1cd17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529481} {:answer/id #uuid "9dc9dfd1-c806-54b0-8fb6-09db505bf845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529490} {:answer/id #uuid "bfa471b8-1af4-56bc-9a31-bd919dc032fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529495} {:answer/id #uuid "fbf3f248-70d6-5ab2-8dca-64f43603e207" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bfa471b8-1af4-56bc-9a31-bd919dc032fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529495} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9d99e66-e5d7-5abb-90a0-6ef8b10366af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529501}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bc7d76dd-c18f-5702-856b-f5311bdfc8e8" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=x - 3 y,$ where $x=- s + 2 t$ and $y=s + t.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/11/118759b163a4410f66d5855d7b7b1fd9c2ee4be585e778a759997036bd95f765.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t)$ and $y=y(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =1, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =2, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t} \\\\  & =(1)\\cdot (2)+(-3)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =(2)+(-3) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529511 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "069ee00b-3b81-58c4-aafb-ac5df45dfb47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sin^{5}{\\alpha}+2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}-3\\cos^{3}{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529506} {:answer/id #uuid "51102831-0b52-55ff-b106-4f8f5c60f7ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}-3\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}\\cos^{3}{\\alpha}+3\\cos^{5}{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529519} {:answer/id #uuid "5a5efeaa-0ca8-5791-b00d-02a60878f45e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}+3\\cos^{3}{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529521} {:answer/id #uuid "64c082c2-46d7-5e51-9b9b-d650e53fbdc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}-3\\cos^{3}{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529523} {:answer/id #uuid "9eb047a5-68f0-571b-8dca-deb7ceb9c09b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}-3\\cos^{3}{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9eb047a5-68f0-571b-8dca-deb7ceb9c09b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}-3\\cos^{3}{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529540} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dbc1be4-16b4-5e63-b06b-5cdf8c3a1d61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529518}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "29ebbec7-da39-54fd-9ec6-bb153c034c9f" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $-2\\sin^{5}{\\alpha}-2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}-3\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}\\cos^{3}{\\alpha}-3\\cos^{5}{\\alpha}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n-2\\sin^{5}{\\alpha}-2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}-3\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}\\cos^{3}{\\alpha}-3\\cos^{5}{\\alpha}=-2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}+\\cos^{2}{\\alpha})-3\\cos^{3}{\\alpha}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}+\\cos^{2}{\\alpha})\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}+\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}+\\cos^{2}{\\alpha})-3\\cos^{3}{\\alpha}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}+\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}) & =-2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}\\cdot 1-3\\cos^{3}{\\alpha}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}-3\\cos^{3}{\\alpha}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-2\\sin^{5}{\\alpha}-2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}-3\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}\\cos^{3}{\\alpha}-3\\cos^{5}{\\alpha}=-2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}-3\\cos^{3}{\\alpha}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529517 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "738330c4-4d5f-5eae-af1b-cfe8981008bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529527} {:answer/id #uuid "754e1324-3526-51e4-9e76-7b633e24a760" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529530} {:answer/id #uuid "e42b7626-cf9c-5708-808c-87b2f0d03244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\sin^{4}{t}\\cos{t}-4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos^{3}{t}+4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529560} {:answer/id #uuid "e824f10c-2194-513f-808f-7584d79a36f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529561} {:answer/id #uuid "edca931a-8d40-5dac-a2c2-71e8b97da970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\sin^{4}{t}\\cos{t}+4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos^{3}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "754e1324-3526-51e4-9e76-7b633e24a760" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529530} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea1a3208-3527-517f-9448-8fb7c165c3ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529562}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3ef681b0-cd16-5bbb-b438-cfbaed372727" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $-4\\sin^{4}{t}\\cos{t}-4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos^{3}{t}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n-4\\sin^{4}{t}\\cos{t}-4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos^{3}{t}=-4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos{t}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{t}+\\cos^{2}{t})\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\sin^{2}{t}+\\cos^{2}{t}=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos{t}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{t}+\\cos^{2}{t}) & =-4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos{t}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-4\\sin^{4}{t}\\cos{t}-4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos^{3}{t}=-4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos{t}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529524 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f156bf3-af81-5a0c-a396-3e3dcc0324cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos{t}-2\\sin{t}+4\\cos^{3}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529532} {:answer/id #uuid "9b2a99ad-92c9-50d3-980a-50d186cbe56d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sin{t}-4\\cos{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529538} {:answer/id #uuid "9dc03acc-2ed8-58cc-8dd3-6760fa6f614a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sin{t}+4\\cos{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529539} {:answer/id #uuid "b85c58fb-5b54-595e-87fa-012036fb6449" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sin^{3}{t}+2\\sin{t}\\cos^{2}{t}-4\\cos{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529547} {:answer/id #uuid "d3f5d711-b02f-5f08-9f78-9612e39f0e89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sin{t}-4\\cos{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529556}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b2a99ad-92c9-50d3-980a-50d186cbe56d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sin{t}-4\\cos{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529538} :answer-field/id #uuid "1276cdc8-bd2f-5e34-80bb-98558c45f158" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529508}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "666f27f4-2d09-51ff-853c-bd215719ca71" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $-2\\sin^{3}{t}-2\\sin{t}\\cos^{2}{t}-4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos{t}-4\\cos^{3}{t}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n-2\\sin^{3}{t}-2\\sin{t}\\cos^{2}{t}-4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos{t}-4\\cos^{3}{t}=-2\\sin{t}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{t}+\\cos^{2}{t})-4\\cos{t}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{t}+\\cos^{2}{t})\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\sin^{2}{t}+\\cos^{2}{t}=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2\\sin{t}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{t}+\\cos^{2}{t})-4\\cos{t}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{t}+\\cos^{2}{t}) & =-2\\sin{t}\\cdot 1-4\\cos{t}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2\\sin{t}-4\\cos{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-2\\sin^{3}{t}-2\\sin{t}\\cos^{2}{t}-4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos{t}-4\\cos^{3}{t}=-2\\sin{t}-4\\cos{t}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529544 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d14dc8e-650b-568c-82d8-d520e06017ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sin^{3}{\\theta}+4\\cos^{3}{\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529513} {:answer/id #uuid "3a0f6e5c-5dfc-5e25-bc4a-f5fc6b08a33f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sin^{3}{\\theta}-4\\cos^{3}{\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529516} {:answer/id #uuid "7449ad0e-dd5c-5706-b13e-50b17a28a093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\sin^{3}{\\theta}-4\\cos^{3}{\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529529} {:answer/id #uuid "8138a85f-31a1-5dc5-97e8-a820e0ba2ab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sin^{5}{\\theta}-4\\sin^{3}{\\theta}\\cos^{2}{\\theta}-4\\cos^{3}{\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529533} {:answer/id #uuid "bc9c46a6-8042-55b2-a60d-de357655dd0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sin^{3}{\\theta}-4\\sin^{2}{\\theta}\\cos^{3}{\\theta}+4\\cos^{5}{\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a0f6e5c-5dfc-5e25-bc4a-f5fc6b08a33f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sin^{3}{\\theta}-4\\cos^{3}{\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529516} :answer-field/id #uuid "56825817-31fb-5f1f-933e-bf1b55452dbe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529520}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "afc41550-d29f-55c2-b1f4-ab3e1639ac16" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $4\\sin^{5}{\\theta}+4\\sin^{3}{\\theta}\\cos^{2}{\\theta}-4\\sin^{2}{\\theta}\\cos^{3}{\\theta}-4\\cos^{5}{\\theta}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n4\\sin^{5}{\\theta}+4\\sin^{3}{\\theta}\\cos^{2}{\\theta}-4\\sin^{2}{\\theta}\\cos^{3}{\\theta}-4\\cos^{5}{\\theta}=4\\sin^{3}{\\theta}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{\\theta}+\\cos^{2}{\\theta})-4\\cos^{3}{\\theta}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{\\theta}+\\cos^{2}{\\theta})\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\sin^{2}{\\theta}+\\cos^{2}{\\theta}=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\sin^{3}{\\theta}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{\\theta}+\\cos^{2}{\\theta})-4\\cos^{3}{\\theta}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{\\theta}+\\cos^{2}{\\theta}) & =4\\sin^{3}{\\theta}\\cdot 1-4\\cos^{3}{\\theta}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4\\sin^{3}{\\theta}-4\\cos^{3}{\\theta}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n4\\sin^{5}{\\theta}+4\\sin^{3}{\\theta}\\cos^{2}{\\theta}-4\\sin^{2}{\\theta}\\cos^{3}{\\theta}-4\\cos^{5}{\\theta}=4\\sin^{3}{\\theta}-4\\cos^{3}{\\theta}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529545 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0647a842-c5bf-5f27-91f8-c209676e7bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529505} {:answer/id #uuid "0dfef94f-a919-5a95-8993-7807c69b6906" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529507} {:answer/id #uuid "8cc356bc-62ee-5a9a-a462-a57bfa02a4fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\sin^{4}{\\alpha}-5\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}+5\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529536} {:answer/id #uuid "c1d87336-ff8a-5303-a940-8b38ad7c2981" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\sin^{4}{\\alpha}+5\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529550} {:answer/id #uuid "faed4766-af3a-5cde-b514-f35ca89e776e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0dfef94f-a919-5a95-8993-7807c69b6906" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529507} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a10a8ad-69b6-5d7d-9515-683ae175b563" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b1aa7d9e-7196-5074-ab5d-16a877939f5e" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $-5\\sin^{4}{\\alpha}-5\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n-5\\sin^{4}{\\alpha}-5\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}=-5\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}+\\cos^{2}{\\alpha})\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}+\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}+\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}) & =-5\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-5\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-5\\sin^{4}{\\alpha}-5\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}=-5\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529551 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c78ccff-14c6-5533-a289-eda1b3b30f84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}+2\\sin{\\alpha}\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}+3\\sin{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529522} {:answer/id #uuid "a2018f64-c3c7-5855-ac38-6e2dcc99f0bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529541} {:answer/id #uuid "b58c94b3-3a3e-5ff8-9a20-f66306bd7d53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529546} {:answer/id #uuid "cd7da2bd-f680-5a24-a57a-44c806b2fb6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\sin{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529554} {:answer/id #uuid "d407429a-0cb9-5745-b7bc-92adb65c01f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sin{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2018f64-c3c7-5855-ac38-6e2dcc99f0bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529541} :answer-field/id #uuid "18153b49-2b8d-5c4d-815e-e3f4cea22382" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529510}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c2187ae7-da6a-5733-bb0f-46f543060cc9" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $-2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}-2\\sin{\\alpha}\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}+3\\sin{\\alpha}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n-2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}-2\\sin{\\alpha}\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}+3\\sin{\\alpha}=-2\\sin{\\alpha}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}+\\cos^{2}{\\alpha})+3\\sin{\\alpha}\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}+\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2\\sin{\\alpha}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}+\\cos^{2}{\\alpha})+3\\sin{\\alpha} & =-2\\sin{\\alpha}\\cdot 1+3\\sin{\\alpha} \\\\  & =-2\\sin{\\alpha}+3\\sin{\\alpha} \\\\  & =\\sin{\\alpha}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}-2\\sin{\\alpha}\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}+3\\sin{\\alpha}=\\sin{\\alpha}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529552 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e6fa6d8-14f9-5d7e-bc0a-c0ac762d492d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sin^{5}{t}+3\\sin^{3}{t}\\cos^{2}{t}+4\\cos{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529531} {:answer/id #uuid "9b2645af-aa72-5f2a-96a8-a02b386cf848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sin^{3}{t}-4\\cos{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529537} {:answer/id #uuid "a9bff1c3-a55f-505a-b6af-8f936dcf6336" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sin^{3}{t}+4\\cos{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529543} {:answer/id #uuid "c71f33ed-a6c3-50f4-af95-943149e25f59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sin^{3}{t}+4\\cos{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529553} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f110f6-d11f-507e-ba9c-4ea58e00874b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sin^{3}{t}+4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos{t}-4\\cos^{3}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c71f33ed-a6c3-50f4-af95-943149e25f59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sin^{3}{t}+4\\cos{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529553} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bd67cb8-bc44-58c2-8091-8061dd78ff1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529534}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c643a2d3-8e99-523f-874d-9db3749f9951" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $-3\\sin^{5}{t}-3\\sin^{3}{t}\\cos^{2}{t}+4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos{t}+4\\cos^{3}{t}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n-3\\sin^{5}{t}-3\\sin^{3}{t}\\cos^{2}{t}+4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos{t}+4\\cos^{3}{t}=-3\\sin^{3}{t}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{t}+\\cos^{2}{t})+4\\cos{t}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{t}+\\cos^{2}{t})\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\sin^{2}{t}+\\cos^{2}{t}=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3\\sin^{3}{t}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{t}+\\cos^{2}{t})+4\\cos{t}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{t}+\\cos^{2}{t}) & =-3\\sin^{3}{t}\\cdot 1+4\\cos{t}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-3\\sin^{3}{t}+4\\cos{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-3\\sin^{5}{t}-3\\sin^{3}{t}\\cos^{2}{t}+4\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos{t}+4\\cos^{3}{t}=-3\\sin^{3}{t}+4\\cos{t}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529559 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13bd1fc4-9eaf-52c2-b404-e2308f82f256" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sin^{3}{x}\\cos^{2}{x}-4\\sin{x}\\cos^{4}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529509} {:answer/id #uuid "7407f81c-8088-5b0b-8bd9-2949a317d2d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\sin{x}\\cos^{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529528} {:answer/id #uuid "8c4d40ec-19ee-53ed-bcce-79179d290ad1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sin^{3}{x}\\cos^{2}{x}+4\\sin{x}\\cos^{4}{x}-4\\sin{x}\\cos^{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529535} {:answer/id #uuid "bca9221d-f021-54c0-9080-6c3992d70ff2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sin{x}\\cos^{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529549} {:answer/id #uuid "f5a80062-0511-5a71-bc83-b69845acfec0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sin{x}\\cos^{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bca9221d-f021-54c0-9080-6c3992d70ff2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sin{x}\\cos^{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529549} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce0cec1e-bfc8-5d38-922f-fa5962556cb1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529555}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de4cfc2b-1f6d-5e13-8785-7726c5e967ba" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $4\\sin^{3}{x}\\cos^{2}{x}+4\\sin{x}\\cos^{4}{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n4\\sin^{3}{x}\\cos^{2}{x}+4\\sin{x}\\cos^{4}{x}=4\\sin{x}\\cos^{2}{x}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{x}+\\cos^{2}{x})\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\sin^{2}{x}+\\cos^{2}{x}=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\sin{x}\\cos^{2}{x}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{x}+\\cos^{2}{x}) & =4\\sin{x}\\cos^{2}{x}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4\\sin{x}\\cos^{2}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n4\\sin^{3}{x}\\cos^{2}{x}+4\\sin{x}\\cos^{4}{x}=4\\sin{x}\\cos^{2}{x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529563 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "373cf1e1-2e2f-53ec-926d-b29631075e7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sin^{3}{t}+\\cos^{3}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529514} {:answer/id #uuid "38170470-3470-577b-aa1d-2853d7b41017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sin^{3}{t}-\\cos^{3}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529515} {:answer/id #uuid "67ee417b-1209-5fd5-95e9-de28b4ecb9f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sin^{3}{t}-\\cos^{3}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529525} {:answer/id #uuid "a279eb83-355b-52c7-8909-482da57bef22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sin^{5}{t}+3\\sin^{3}{t}\\cos^{2}{t}-\\cos^{3}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529542} {:answer/id #uuid "d895177c-6aa9-517e-a66e-17e8de422018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sin^{3}{t}-\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos^{3}{t}+\\cos^{5}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529558}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67ee417b-1209-5fd5-95e9-de28b4ecb9f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sin^{3}{t}-\\cos^{3}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529525} :answer-field/id #uuid "710c80ef-9c4c-5aef-9254-157853bfdaac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "edb7022c-1785-5002-946d-38c55cec59ac" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $-3\\sin^{5}{t}-3\\sin^{3}{t}\\cos^{2}{t}-\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos^{3}{t}-\\cos^{5}{t}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n-3\\sin^{5}{t}-3\\sin^{3}{t}\\cos^{2}{t}-\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos^{3}{t}-\\cos^{5}{t}=-3\\sin^{3}{t}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{t}+\\cos^{2}{t})-\\cos^{3}{t}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{t}+\\cos^{2}{t})\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\sin^{2}{t}+\\cos^{2}{t}=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3\\sin^{3}{t}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{t}+\\cos^{2}{t})-\\cos^{3}{t}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{t}+\\cos^{2}{t}) & =-3\\sin^{3}{t}\\cdot 1-\\cos^{3}{t}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-3\\sin^{3}{t}-\\cos^{3}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-3\\sin^{5}{t}-3\\sin^{3}{t}\\cos^{2}{t}-\\sin^{2}{t}\\cos^{3}{t}-\\cos^{5}{t}=-3\\sin^{3}{t}-\\cos^{3}{t}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530432 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49976768-431c-507e-a6c7-d2d95eebbbf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529754} {:answer/id #uuid "58bb366b-a9d7-55ba-9cad-0fd6b63a25f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529793} {:answer/id #uuid "5b93773f-b140-52dc-ab08-af172348d56d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529801} {:answer/id #uuid "e0f729d2-960c-5f9c-be65-97c3cbad4b0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530141} {:answer/id #uuid "e73ba0dc-dc17-54e6-8c52-71c213062fd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b93773f-b140-52dc-ab08-af172348d56d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529801} :answer-field/id #uuid "90762acc-754a-5149-93b4-5bc79b9c05e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "20cfcb32-46de-59b7-8990-d20e7a58a53a" :question/math-academy-id "q-36467" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $c=0$ gives two lines\n\nII. $c=1$ gives a circle\n\nIII. $c=2$ gives a hyperbola" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=0$ the level curves are $y=\\pm 2x,$ which consists of two lines.\n\n- If $c=1$ the level curve is $4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=1,$ which is a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=2$ the level curve is $2{x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1,$ which is a hyperbola.\n\nSo, only statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530438 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b8518d8-9401-5fbb-80b4-3637c13a5c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/84/844b92278c8b945a68104629b8dcb14d1b41c6875677ffda4da9615363e55221.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529800} {:answer/id #uuid "af41d1db-4df3-5f82-8a52-be9e6a8e128a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/82/824e2fb10927e9ac63fc6e57c15efb94af3100d89a06db8bad63752e232e5a7b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530017} {:answer/id #uuid "f7438267-12f3-5bc5-8c7f-3213295c7e92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/92/9259f6992539edaa9997b167a894fcd8f60ec25978a6bf0c6d7e70b46a5bc056.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530194} {:answer/id #uuid "f930bbbc-48b4-54bf-8000-807c4b6018dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fa/fa880cc10c7f9f1532e4fd92093b8d9ff47ab32a220a2c4277ecccabb6788334.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530198} {:answer/id #uuid "f978f806-3849-540f-afee-4d73d3644018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/81/81e763cf8b1bf3a6cd2681876642778e97eb4db915373cd07149c42b2e424c65.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b8518d8-9401-5fbb-80b4-3637c13a5c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/84/844b92278c8b945a68104629b8dcb14d1b41c6875677ffda4da9615363e55221.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529800} :answer-field/id #uuid "41ce99e3-3910-54c5-acc5-a4b9b347da9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530264}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "248c7282-1f4b-5be4-93d4-cb424b9138b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-64978" :question/problem "![](images/63/634a863f2154398762af17da40b22d303b10b8846c90fa2021148779e1d1fa97.png)\n\nWhich of the following could represent the level curves of the surface $z=2{x}^{2}$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $[0,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider only $c$-level curves for $c\\ge 0.$\n\nThe level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =c \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{c}{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that in the equations $x=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{c}{2}}$ do not depend on $y.$ So, for a given $c\\ge 0$, the right-hand side of the equation is constant. As a result, we obtain a family of vertical lines, as shown below.\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/84/844b92278c8b945a68104629b8dcb14d1b41c6875677ffda4da9615363e55221.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532677 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fd0fc7c-99d8-5050-a35b-ea1c9e5595da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{e}^{y}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531962} {:answer/id #uuid "16b1ed05-f11e-5af1-bc34-24beec772bad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy-{e}^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531978} {:answer/id #uuid "36ad00a7-4313-5719-9082-bbc20b1b1a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{y}-{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532044} {:answer/id #uuid "c3f11af5-f6e7-587e-ad2a-37a69de5389a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(2y-{e}^{y})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532354} {:answer/id #uuid "db6bfd8c-6f2d-50b7-aeb8-7a436d51fb24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{y}-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3f11af5-f6e7-587e-ad2a-37a69de5389a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(2y-{e}^{y})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532354} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8115568-baaa-5b24-a293-0a1071a31bac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532602}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8a8ebfaa-e511-5ff1-bf18-6d98ce82aec8" :question/math-academy-id "q-126531" :question/problem "Given that $F(x,y)=x{e}^{y}\\,i+y{x}^{2}\\,j,$ what is the scalar curl of $F?$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y{x}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{y}) \\\\  & =2xy-x{e}^{y} \\\\  & =x(2y-{e}^{y}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186532776 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0505bfb8-fbfd-554c-8e3d-44ac942e0b16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532769} {:answer/id #uuid "38be668d-9ab7-5436-b034-cb331b91c492" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0505bfb8-fbfd-554c-8e3d-44ac942e0b16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532769} :answer-field/id #uuid "5de480c0-0dd0-5de8-af4e-b39414765809" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532774} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83d545a1-3cb7-50ad-afd2-99914e5c776e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532777} {:answer/id #uuid "e99e88eb-25ca-5d9e-a643-ad008b0e980a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532780}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e99e88eb-25ca-5d9e-a643-ad008b0e980a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532780} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b93784d-4281-5760-8eef-4865819e8b08" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532775} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "088fe0c1-c315-512f-86fb-109ae98d416a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532771} {:answer/id #uuid "f1bf54e5-cbe9-579a-a9d4-b978428e5567" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1bf54e5-cbe9-579a-a9d4-b978428e5567" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532781} :answer-field/id #uuid "902b4a07-6d8b-5503-adc1-c2e50d71cada" :answer-field/key "$\\text{curl}\\,F=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532778} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "072a3f6e-5df0-5342-bc7b-11b9d8003818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532770} {:answer/id #uuid "19cc02c5-93de-526b-a4a3-d3c40f42c505" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19cc02c5-93de-526b-a4a3-d3c40f42c505" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532772} :answer-field/id #uuid "d88cb888-c4d7-5ba8-baab-76faa9062e42" :answer-field/key "$F$ is irrotational" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186532779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7f1277c2-1732-59aa-9938-5b092ddfb7eb" :question/problem "![](images/ac/ac756d7cbd687a23a5b2c1ffcb368298f4676178e8bebccbadd4e837fe66a3d7.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y,z),$ shown above. Given that $F(x,y,z)$ is independent of $z,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{curl}\\,F$ denotes the curl of the vector field $F.$\n\nTo understand intuitively whether a vector field has curl at a point $P$, imagine that $F$ represents the velocity field of flowing water. Place a paddlewheel at $P$ with its axis in the $z$-direction. If it rotates, the field has nonzero curl; if it does not, the field has zero curl.\n\nThe arrows turn a paddlewheel counterclockwise. Thus $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$ throughout space, so $F$ is not irrotational. Curl measures local rotation, even when the arrows also spread outward. Wrap the fingers of your right hand in the counterclockwise direction: your thumb points out of the screen, in the positive $z$-direction.\n\nWith that in mind, check each statement:\n\n- Statement $\\text{curl}\\,F=0$ is false.\n- Statement $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$ is true.\n- Statement “$F$ is irrotational” is false.\n- Statement “$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction” is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{curl}\\,F\\ne 0$; “$\\text{curl}\\,F$ points in the positive $z$-direction” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533019 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cb970e3-fec2-59c3-a6ab-a3da31447c6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv - 2 u + 4 v^{2} + 2 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533016} {:answer/id #uuid "40978c7c-ce5d-5547-abec-9a813dd99da4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 10 uv + 4 v^{2} + 4 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533030} {:answer/id #uuid "4ff527fd-9ade-5e4f-b140-6b410e0a8d2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv + 4 v^{2} + 4 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533039} {:answer/id #uuid "8bae58cd-5720-56b2-94f7-ffdee9f864dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 u^{2} v + 8 uv^{2} + 6 uv - 4 v^{2} - 4 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533054} {:answer/id #uuid "ebdb7518-cf53-5938-8511-2fc4d8f960f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 u^{2} v + 8 uv^{2} + 10 uv + 4 u - 4 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ff527fd-9ade-5e4f-b140-6b410e0a8d2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv + 4 v^{2} + 4 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533039} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fccb2ba-6b05-5811-b0e6-c1883ffe52db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533060}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "242f9872-bf27-5e8a-81c2-046ba61bdf6d" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨2 z,\\,2 xy,\\,2 x + 2 y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=2 xy + x - y$ for $0\\le x\\le 3$ and $0\\le y\\le 4.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,2 uv + u - v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 3,\\,0\\le v\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2 uv + u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2 v + 1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2 uv + u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2 u - 1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 v + 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 u - 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 v + 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 v + 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 2 v - 1,\\,1 - 2 u,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨2 z,\\,2 xy,\\,2 x + 2 y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=2 uv + u - v} \\\\  & =⟨2 (2 uv + u - v),\\,2 uv,\\,2 u + 2 v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4 uv + 2 u - 2 v,\\,2 uv,\\,2 u + 2 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨4 uv + 2 u - 2 v,\\,2 uv,\\,2 u + 2 v⟩\\cdot ⟨- 2 v - 1,\\,1 - 2 u,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(4 uv + 2 u - 2 v)\\cdot (- 2 v - 1)+(2 uv)\\cdot (1 - 2 u)+(2 u + 2 v)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =- 8 uv^{2} - 8 uv - 2 u + 4 v^{2} + 2 v- 4 u^{2} v + 2 uv+2 u + 2 v \\\\  & =- 4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv + 4 v^{2} + 4 v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨2 z,\\,2 xy,\\,2 x + 2 y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(- 4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv + 4 v^{2} + 4 v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}(- 4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv + 4 v^{2} + 4 v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533020 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d7a8d4c-4e17-5501-8857-53f3be2da1d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 u^{2} v + uv^{2} - u + v^{2} - v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533014} {:answer/id #uuid "3cc755dc-f887-5272-97f5-4b9a2c9c3ecb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 u^{2} v - uv^{2} - 4 uv + u - v^{2} + v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533025} {:answer/id #uuid "4f5ee7a8-25b7-5f0f-8fb3-0262cf50375a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 u^{2} v - uv^{2} + u - v^{2} + v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533038} {:answer/id #uuid "b1f1a002-0ad3-585c-a03c-c4156253e284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 u^{2} v + uv^{2} + 4 uv + 3 u + v^{2} + 3 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533064} {:answer/id #uuid "ef98e849-0030-5ffd-8149-2a1ca47cec56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 u^{2} v - uv^{2} - u - v^{2} - v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f5ee7a8-25b7-5f0f-8fb3-0262cf50375a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 u^{2} v - uv^{2} + u - v^{2} + v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533038} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c81baa9-1eb1-5b7e-ae50-be3131b6b8c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533034}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "321ff97a-842a-5d43-bdf8-efb78e10b9c5" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,2 xy,\\,2 x + 2 y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=- xy - x - y$ for $-3\\le x\\le 4$ and $-2\\le y\\le 4.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{-3}^{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,- uv - u - v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-3\\le u\\le 4,\\,-2\\le v\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(- uv - u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,- v - 1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(- uv - u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,- u - 1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & - v - 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & - u - 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & - v - 1 \\\\ 1 & - u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & - v - 1 \\\\ 0 & - u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨v + 1,\\,u + 1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z,\\,2 xy,\\,2 x + 2 y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=- uv - u - v} \\\\  & =⟨(- uv - u - v),\\,2 uv,\\,2 u + 2 v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- uv - u - v,\\,2 uv,\\,2 u + 2 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨- uv - u - v,\\,2 uv,\\,2 u + 2 v⟩\\cdot ⟨v + 1,\\,u + 1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(- uv - u - v)\\cdot (v + 1)+(2 uv)\\cdot (u + 1)+(2 u + 2 v)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =- uv^{2} - 2 uv - u - v^{2} - v+2 u^{2} v + 2 uv+2 u + 2 v \\\\  & =2 u^{2} v - uv^{2} + u - v^{2} + v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,2 xy,\\,2 x + 2 y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2 u^{2} v - uv^{2} + u - v^{2} + v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}(2 u^{2} v - uv^{2} + u - v^{2} + v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533024 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0932a0b8-0fa3-568b-8122-0d1797e9cf4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 u^{2} + 2 uv + 3 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533013} {:answer/id #uuid "3e72d819-13b8-5082-b185-e39011021788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 u^{2} - 2 uv - 3 v^{2} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533028} {:answer/id #uuid "58b973af-0382-5e69-80b6-ea466d6662d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 u^{2} - 6 uv + v^{2} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533042} {:answer/id #uuid "75cd9606-d654-52a8-a5df-a87da24d8731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 u^{2} - 2 uv - 2 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533049} {:answer/id #uuid "ee47443a-eea8-51b0-9a9a-89c398f06335" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u^{2} + 6 uv - 3 v^{2} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e72d819-13b8-5082-b185-e39011021788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 u^{2} - 2 uv - 3 v^{2} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533028} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f7dc13a-554c-5bca-a074-a38d478e5b34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533050}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3a7156dc-8a49-52bc-98b0-49852881e07e" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x + 2 y,\\,- x + y,\\,2 - z⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=x^{2} + y^{2}$ for $1\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 4.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{4}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u^{2} + v^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u^{2} + v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2 u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u^{2} + v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 u \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 u \\\\ 1 & 2 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 u \\\\ 0 & 2 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 2 u,\\,- 2 v,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x + 2 y,\\,- x + y,\\,2 - z⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=u^{2} + v^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨u + 2 v,\\,- u + v,\\,2 - (u^{2} + v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u + 2 v,\\,- u + v,\\,- u^{2} - v^{2} + 2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u + 2 v,\\,- u + v,\\,- u^{2} - v^{2} + 2⟩\\cdot ⟨- 2 u,\\,- 2 v,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u + 2 v)\\cdot (- 2 u)+(- u + v)\\cdot (- 2 v)+(- u^{2} - v^{2} + 2)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =- 2 u^{2} - 4 uv+2 uv - 2 v^{2}- u^{2} - v^{2} + 2 \\\\  & =- 3 u^{2} - 2 uv - 3 v^{2} + 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x + 2 y,\\,- x + y,\\,2 - z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(- 3 u^{2} - 2 uv - 3 v^{2} + 2)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{4}(- 3 u^{2} - 2 uv - 3 v^{2} + 2)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533026 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36a9ae0c-05c2-5810-b015-e97301bea69e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 10 uv - u - 4 v^{2} - v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533021} {:answer/id #uuid "87acc8e3-7bc7-5f02-9f26-1cb953a6440f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv - 2 u - 4 v^{2} - 2 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533053} {:answer/id #uuid "8c05f39c-15f2-58ce-a3e4-102d3539e0b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv - u - 4 v^{2} - v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533055} {:answer/id #uuid "c76e5c07-3121-53e1-825f-0413889dd45d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 u^{2} v + 8 uv^{2} + 10 uv + 3 u + 4 v^{2} + 3 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533070} {:answer/id #uuid "ffa7c823-f513-584f-ad63-a1f5646d5e27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 u^{2} v + 8 uv^{2} + 6 uv + u + 4 v^{2} + v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c05f39c-15f2-58ce-a3e4-102d3539e0b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv - u - 4 v^{2} - v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533055} :answer-field/id #uuid "a21209f7-71c6-5bfe-99c1-c5b2cccfb0bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533061}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3e4db5c4-da60-5458-9dd4-b7ca956bf947" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨2 z,\\,2 xy,\\,x + y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=- 2 xy - x - y$ for $1\\le x\\le 4$ and $-1\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,- 2 uv - u - v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 4,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(- 2 uv - u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,- 2 v - 1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(- 2 uv - u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,- 2 u - 1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & - 2 v - 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & - 2 u - 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & - 2 v - 1 \\\\ 1 & - 2 u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & - 2 v - 1 \\\\ 0 & - 2 u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 v + 1,\\,2 u + 1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨2 z,\\,2 xy,\\,x + y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=- 2 uv - u - v} \\\\  & =⟨2 (- 2 uv - u - v),\\,2 uv,\\,u + v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 4 uv - 2 u - 2 v,\\,2 uv,\\,u + v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨- 4 uv - 2 u - 2 v,\\,2 uv,\\,u + v⟩\\cdot ⟨2 v + 1,\\,2 u + 1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(- 4 uv - 2 u - 2 v)\\cdot (2 v + 1)+(2 uv)\\cdot (2 u + 1)+(u + v)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =- 8 uv^{2} - 8 uv - 2 u - 4 v^{2} - 2 v+4 u^{2} v + 2 uv+u + v \\\\  & =4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv - u - 4 v^{2} - v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨2 z,\\,2 xy,\\,x + y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv - u - 4 v^{2} - v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv - u - 4 v^{2} - v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533035 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ab142e5-68b6-5e46-85e2-53b0af63f72f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 u^{2} v - 4 uv^{2} + 3 uv + 2 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533015} {:answer/id #uuid "38d189a3-49d7-562c-a5a8-dff53a82b5e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 u^{2} v - 4 uv^{2} + 5 uv - u + 2 v^{2} - v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533022} {:answer/id #uuid "3e618450-6c32-50ee-9891-cb5a7053df4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 u^{2} v + 4 uv^{2} - 5 uv - 2 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533027} {:answer/id #uuid "55297ea1-0c27-5ad6-8719-ac0395fb8a02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 u^{2} v - 4 uv^{2} + 5 uv + 2 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533041} {:answer/id #uuid "9a18d3bd-dd38-5d10-9ccb-e45362470b35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 u^{2} v + 4 uv^{2} - 3 uv + 2 u - 2 v^{2} + 2 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55297ea1-0c27-5ad6-8719-ac0395fb8a02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 u^{2} v - 4 uv^{2} + 5 uv + 2 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533041} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebd73cc3-9cb5-5ff2-8ee0-589c4c8b7073" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533074}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4cc0069f-c627-527a-995d-c48582128901" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,xy,\\,x + y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=2 xy - x - y$ for $0\\le x\\le 4$ and $0\\le y\\le 3.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,2 uv - u - v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 4,\\,0\\le v\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2 uv - u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2 v - 1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2 uv - u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2 u - 1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 v - 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 u - 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 v - 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 v - 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1 - 2 v,\\,1 - 2 u,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z,\\,xy,\\,x + y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=2 uv - u - v} \\\\  & =⟨(2 uv - u - v),\\,uv,\\,u + v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 uv - u - v,\\,uv,\\,u + v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨2 uv - u - v,\\,uv,\\,u + v⟩\\cdot ⟨1 - 2 v,\\,1 - 2 u,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(2 uv - u - v)\\cdot (1 - 2 v)+(uv)\\cdot (1 - 2 u)+(u + v)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =- 4 uv^{2} + 4 uv - u + 2 v^{2} - v- 2 u^{2} v + uv+u + v \\\\  & =- 2 u^{2} v - 4 uv^{2} + 5 uv + 2 v^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,xy,\\,x + y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(- 2 u^{2} v - 4 uv^{2} + 5 uv + 2 v^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(- 2 u^{2} v - 4 uv^{2} + 5 uv + 2 v^{2})\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533036 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7436a512-84c9-591c-9ce9-fcc70e1d47ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 u^{2} + 8 uv + 2 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533046} {:answer/id #uuid "8f050df9-ff08-51a6-b322-512385345065" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 u^{2} - 8 uv - 3 v^{2} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533056} {:answer/id #uuid "a8b6cc4a-eef9-568d-bb45-387ac415e38c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 u^{2} - v^{2} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533062} {:answer/id #uuid "da71da48-1d04-5e46-96ca-c7e90bbff07c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 u^{2} + 3 v^{2} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533073} {:answer/id #uuid "f2b20ec7-b848-5947-b64a-04215b62f1b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 u^{2} + 8 uv + 3 v^{2} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533078}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2b20ec7-b848-5947-b64a-04215b62f1b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 u^{2} + 8 uv + 3 v^{2} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533078} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf94c05a-12ff-5582-8b0f-1126b1a459c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4ed6e5af-2150-51ed-b676-4ac61ca8579d" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x + y,\\,2 x + y,\\,- z - 1⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=- 2 x^{2} - y^{2}$ for $1\\le x\\le 4$ and $-1\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,- 2 u^{2} - v^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 4,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(- 2 u^{2} - v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,- 4 u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(- 2 u^{2} - v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,- 2 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & - 4 u \\\\ 0 & 1 & - 2 v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & - 4 u \\\\ 1 & - 2 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & - 4 u \\\\ 0 & - 2 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4 u,\\,2 v,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x + y,\\,2 x + y,\\,- z - 1⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=- 2 u^{2} - v^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨u + v,\\,2 u + v,\\,- (- 2 u^{2} - v^{2}) - 1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u + v,\\,2 u + v,\\,2 u^{2} + v^{2} - 1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u + v,\\,2 u + v,\\,2 u^{2} + v^{2} - 1⟩\\cdot ⟨4 u,\\,2 v,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u + v)\\cdot (4 u)+(2 u + v)\\cdot (2 v)+(2 u^{2} + v^{2} - 1)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =4 u^{2} + 4 uv+4 uv + 2 v^{2}+2 u^{2} + v^{2} - 1 \\\\  & =6 u^{2} + 8 uv + 3 v^{2} - 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x + y,\\,2 x + y,\\,- z - 1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(6 u^{2} + 8 uv + 3 v^{2} - 1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(6 u^{2} + 8 uv + 3 v^{2} - 1)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533048 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03138265-2aad-5cac-aea7-3cb673bb03f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 u^{2} - 6 uv + 10 v^{2} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533011} {:answer/id #uuid "2118e949-0da7-5604-af88-a5a5bfc91e01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 u^{2} - 6 uv + 12 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533018} {:answer/id #uuid "40914390-37f2-59aa-a6d7-afabccbbdd5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 5 u^{2} + 6 uv - 10 v^{2} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533029} {:answer/id #uuid "745222d1-5f79-5053-a65b-b50ff6270bc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 7 u^{2} - 2 uv + 10 v^{2} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533047} {:answer/id #uuid "f818a851-f2af-5d62-ae5d-ad9d62e92dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 u^{2} + 2 uv - 14 v^{2} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03138265-2aad-5cac-aea7-3cb673bb03f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 u^{2} - 6 uv + 10 v^{2} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533011} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d6e7828-aa1e-5e60-961d-f41de42d5c51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533044}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "74c1515c-d50d-5d9f-a7b8-3c0f3e090bb9" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨3 x - y,\\,- x + 3 y,\\,z + 1⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=- x^{2} - 2 y^{2}$ for $-3\\le x\\le 4$ and $-2\\le y\\le 4.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{-3}^{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,- u^{2} - 2 v^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-3\\le u\\le 4,\\,-2\\le v\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(- u^{2} - 2 v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,- 2 u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(- u^{2} - 2 v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,- 4 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & - 2 u \\\\ 0 & 1 & - 4 v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & - 2 u \\\\ 1 & - 4 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & - 2 u \\\\ 0 & - 4 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 u,\\,4 v,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨3 x - y,\\,- x + 3 y,\\,z + 1⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=- u^{2} - 2 v^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨3 u - v,\\,- u + 3 v,\\,(- u^{2} - 2 v^{2}) + 1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3 u - v,\\,- u + 3 v,\\,- u^{2} - 2 v^{2} + 1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3 u - v,\\,- u + 3 v,\\,- u^{2} - 2 v^{2} + 1⟩\\cdot ⟨2 u,\\,4 v,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(3 u - v)\\cdot (2 u)+(- u + 3 v)\\cdot (4 v)+(- u^{2} - 2 v^{2} + 1)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =6 u^{2} - 2 uv- 4 uv + 12 v^{2}- u^{2} - 2 v^{2} + 1 \\\\  & =5 u^{2} - 6 uv + 10 v^{2} + 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3 x - y,\\,- x + 3 y,\\,z + 1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5 u^{2} - 6 uv + 10 v^{2} + 1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}(5 u^{2} - 6 uv + 10 v^{2} + 1)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533051 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20356f6f-b037-59be-966f-b091b3698cf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 uv + 8 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533017} {:answer/id #uuid "54edc1d0-d27e-5dd3-b36d-d7f4051319b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 uv + 4 v^{2} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533040} {:answer/id #uuid "822197f9-d002-5835-967e-4c1e3dcf83c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 u^{2} - 12 uv - 6 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533052} {:answer/id #uuid "c24b954e-bdab-5c9a-a900-aa62e0e16490" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 u^{2} + 4 uv - 4 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533068} {:answer/id #uuid "cc77d781-d951-5e29-9131-3809cfe9f578" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 uv - 4 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc77d781-d951-5e29-9131-3809cfe9f578" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 uv - 4 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533071} :answer-field/id #uuid "acf7f6e2-91ba-5169-9992-db0e3909a286" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533063}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "80291a1c-e4f6-54f8-83dc-c6ce18ed1635" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x + 2 y,\\,2 x + 3 y,\\,2 z - 2⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=2 x^{2} + y^{2}$ for $0\\le x\\le 3$ and $0\\le y\\le 4.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,2 u^{2} + v^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 3,\\,0\\le v\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2 u^{2} + v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,4 u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2 u^{2} + v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 u \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 u \\\\ 1 & 2 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 u \\\\ 0 & 2 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 4 u,\\,- 2 v,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x + 2 y,\\,2 x + 3 y,\\,2 z - 2⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=2 u^{2} + v^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨u + 2 v,\\,2 u + 3 v,\\,2 (2 u^{2} + v^{2}) - 2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u + 2 v,\\,2 u + 3 v,\\,4 u^{2} + 2 v^{2} - 2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u + 2 v,\\,2 u + 3 v,\\,4 u^{2} + 2 v^{2} - 2⟩\\cdot ⟨- 4 u,\\,- 2 v,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u + 2 v)\\cdot (- 4 u)+(2 u + 3 v)\\cdot (- 2 v)+(4 u^{2} + 2 v^{2} - 2)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =- 4 u^{2} - 8 uv- 4 uv - 6 v^{2}+4 u^{2} + 2 v^{2} - 2 \\\\  & =- 12 uv - 4 v^{2} - 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x + 2 y,\\,2 x + 3 y,\\,2 z - 2⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(- 12 uv - 4 v^{2} - 2)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}(- 12 uv - 4 v^{2} - 2)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533059 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07f9a1aa-a390-574f-b1d7-d8bb1b97478b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10 u^{2} - 12 uv + 6 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533012} {:answer/id #uuid "4134b830-3887-598c-b479-3d8b85171c5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14 u^{2} + 4 uv - 6 v^{2} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533031} {:answer/id #uuid "995a8e1a-95c0-5a99-b35d-f82c3964898a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 u^{2} - 4 uv + 4 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533057} {:answer/id #uuid "b48be496-3e3d-53b0-838c-eb6f4a85833a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 14 u^{2} - 4 uv + 6 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533065} {:answer/id #uuid "c2fb8c43-78cf-570a-b762-20d95c71474e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 14 u^{2} + 12 uv - 2 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b48be496-3e3d-53b0-838c-eb6f4a85833a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 14 u^{2} - 4 uv + 6 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533065} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f31fcc4-3134-5b21-936a-7d9e43b33462" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533037}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a222f71-5c1c-5947-8337-693d72d6ebf9" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨3 x - y,\\,- 2 x + y,\\,- z - 2⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=2 x^{2} - 2 y^{2}$ for $0\\le x\\le 4$ and $0\\le y\\le 3.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,2 u^{2} - 2 v^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 4,\\,0\\le v\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2 u^{2} - 2 v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,4 u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2 u^{2} - 2 v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,- 4 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 u \\\\ 0 & 1 & - 4 v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 u \\\\ 1 & - 4 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 u \\\\ 0 & - 4 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 4 u,\\,4 v,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨3 x - y,\\,- 2 x + y,\\,- z - 2⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=2 u^{2} - 2 v^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨3 u - v,\\,- 2 u + v,\\,- (2 u^{2} - 2 v^{2}) - 2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3 u - v,\\,- 2 u + v,\\,- 2 u^{2} + 2 v^{2} - 2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3 u - v,\\,- 2 u + v,\\,- 2 u^{2} + 2 v^{2} - 2⟩\\cdot ⟨- 4 u,\\,4 v,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(3 u - v)\\cdot (- 4 u)+(- 2 u + v)\\cdot (4 v)+(- 2 u^{2} + 2 v^{2} - 2)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =- 12 u^{2} + 4 uv- 8 uv + 4 v^{2}- 2 u^{2} + 2 v^{2} - 2 \\\\  & =- 14 u^{2} - 4 uv + 6 v^{2} - 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3 x - y,\\,- 2 x + y,\\,- z - 2⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(- 14 u^{2} - 4 uv + 6 v^{2} - 2)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(- 14 u^{2} - 4 uv + 6 v^{2} - 2)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533067 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "397a6974-dfac-52d9-b5df-0bc50361c68f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u^{2} v + 2 uv^{2} + 3 uv + u - 2 v^{2} - 3 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533023} {:answer/id #uuid "4c6a532c-55a0-59d5-b070-81878ff0060b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- u^{2} v + 2 uv^{2} + 5 uv + 3 u - 2 v^{2} - v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533033} {:answer/id #uuid "5b47b261-eaca-5315-bc67-d920b7c6ebbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u^{2} v - 2 uv^{2} - 5 uv - u + 2 v^{2} + 3 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533043} {:answer/id #uuid "661f9953-9c2c-5019-8928-9710c30593ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- u^{2} v - 2 uv^{2} - 3 uv - u + 2 v^{2} + 3 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533045} {:answer/id #uuid "b4aae3d5-7110-5af4-87b3-e390ceb9db25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- u^{2} v - 2 uv^{2} - 3 uv - 2 u + 2 v^{2} + 2 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "661f9953-9c2c-5019-8928-9710c30593ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- u^{2} v - 2 uv^{2} - 3 uv - u + 2 v^{2} + 3 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533045} :answer-field/id #uuid "460785b5-dfe6-5ff3-bd84-f6157544bae8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533032}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bbbc0ee0-272c-53fb-9af1-c9190cd9e631" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨2 z,\\,xy,\\,x + y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=xy + x - y$ for $1\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 4.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{4}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,uv + u - v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv + u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,v + 1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv + u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,u - 1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & v + 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & u - 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & v + 1 \\\\ 1 & u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & v + 1 \\\\ 0 & u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- v - 1,\\,1 - u,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨2 z,\\,xy,\\,x + y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=uv + u - v} \\\\  & =⟨2 (uv + u - v),\\,uv,\\,u + v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 uv + 2 u - 2 v,\\,uv,\\,u + v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨2 uv + 2 u - 2 v,\\,uv,\\,u + v⟩\\cdot ⟨- v - 1,\\,1 - u,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(2 uv + 2 u - 2 v)\\cdot (- v - 1)+(uv)\\cdot (1 - u)+(u + v)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =- 2 uv^{2} - 4 uv - 2 u + 2 v^{2} + 2 v- u^{2} v + uv+u + v \\\\  & =- u^{2} v - 2 uv^{2} - 3 uv - u + 2 v^{2} + 3 v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨2 z,\\,xy,\\,x + y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(- u^{2} v - 2 uv^{2} - 3 uv - u + 2 v^{2} + 3 v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{4}(- u^{2} v - 2 uv^{2} - 3 uv - u + 2 v^{2} + 3 v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534178 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0df58327-4c7b-56a6-a555-7f93859ea5c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\sqrt{17041}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534180} {:answer/id #uuid "194cc645-b463-5b8e-b9e5-27852c3d7f61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{393}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534183} {:answer/id #uuid "402af249-7f17-5997-9c72-8726a45d2b0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{393}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534187} {:answer/id #uuid "89913d7f-56a6-5fa1-8909-5022b2fa3801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1873917}{1000}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534195} {:answer/id #uuid "99c54e4c-1cdd-56bc-b87f-085bc3821f2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{393}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99c54e4c-1cdd-56bc-b87f-085bc3821f2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{393}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534197} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7c29cac-8af6-5168-a467-de45c5d34de2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "04a33944-3b1f-5a14-b50e-bd7ec0252827" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $$\n\\displaystyle r(t)=\\langle 6 t + 4,- \\frac{\\left(3 t + 2\\right)^{3}}{3} - \\frac{1}{3 t + 2}\\rangle\n$$ from $t=0$ to $t=1$.\n\n![](images/db/db3e582e3cbf491015aa1f08ac77ddb6b02b2a8143bebc2d76d171ebd64f9570.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t)&=\\left\\langle\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(6 t + 4),\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- \\frac{\\left(3 t + 2\\right)^{3}}{3} - \\frac{1}{3 t + 2})\\right\\rangle \\\\ &=\\left\\langle 6,- 3 \\left(3 t + 2\\right)^{2} + \\frac{3}{\\left(3 t + 2\\right)^{2}}\\right\\rangle \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(6)^2+(- 3 \\left(3 t + 2\\right)^{2} + \\frac{3}{\\left(3 t + 2\\right)^{2}})^2} \\\\ &=3\\sqrt{4+\\left(\\frac{1}{(3 t + 2)^2}-(3 t + 2)^2\\right)^2} \\\\ &=3\\sqrt{4+\\frac{1}{(3 t + 2)^4}-2+(3 t + 2)^4} \\\\ &=3\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{(3 t + 2)^4}+2+(3 t + 2)^4} \\\\ &=3\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1}{(3 t + 2)^2}+(3 t + 2)^2\\right)^2} \\\\ &=3 \\left(3 t + 2\\right)^{2} + \\frac{3}{\\left(3 t + 2\\right)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $3 t + 2>0$ throughout the given interval.\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=3 t + 2$, $\\mathrm{d}u=3\\mathrm{d}t$.\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{0}^{1}3 \\left(3 t + 2\\right)^{2} + \\frac{3}{\\left(3 t + 2\\right)^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{2}^{5}u^{2} + \\frac{1}{u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ &=\\frac{u^{3}}{3} - \\frac{1}{u}\\big|_{2}^{5} \\\\ &=1\\left[\\left(-\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{5^3}{3}\\right)-\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{2^3}{3}\\right)\\right] \\\\ &=\\frac{393}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534184 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "250b117a-1a6e-5a97-b059-769051e15c4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\sqrt{13} \\left(1 - e^{2}\\right) e^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534185} {:answer/id #uuid "2a8b2ed2-d752-595e-b229-43faa8ead647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\left(e^{4} \\sin{\\left(6 \\right)} - e^{2} \\sin{\\left(3 \\right)}\\right)^{2} + \\left(- e^{2} \\cos{\\left(3 \\right)} + e^{4} \\cos{\\left(6 \\right)}\\right)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534186} {:answer/id #uuid "9b18cb94-b1cb-5ad4-a330-0b4d0325ea69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\sqrt{13} \\left(1 - e^{2}\\right) e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534198} {:answer/id #uuid "d11d563b-0195-5603-82cd-d4744a5bb965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\sqrt{13} \\left(1 - e^{2}\\right) e^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534205} {:answer/id #uuid "f543d6ec-b86e-5e29-ac6b-e8d6521b7727" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{13 \\left(1 - e^{4}\\right) e^{4}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "250b117a-1a6e-5a97-b059-769051e15c4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\sqrt{13} \\left(1 - e^{2}\\right) e^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534185} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5c8ee22-a23b-516d-bac4-8d5a369d549a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "20f13bd9-c6e7-5a54-a323-8935bc01727e" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $r(t)=\\langle e^{2 t} \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)},e^{2 t} \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\rangle$ from $t=1$ to $t=2$.\n\n![](images/30/3043adc931d85fe438a292b833ad93e601e50da4ca4c4a1d18d27d932e2e0ccc.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t)&=\\left\\langle\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(e^{2 t} \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}),\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(e^{2 t} \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)})\\right\\rangle \\\\ &=\\left\\langle - 3 e^{2 t} \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 2 e^{2 t} \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)},2 e^{2 t} \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 3 e^{2 t} \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right\\rangle \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(- 3 e^{2 t} \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 2 e^{2 t} \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)})^2+(2 e^{2 t} \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 3 e^{2 t} \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)})^2} \\\\ &=e^{2 t}\\sqrt{(2\\cos(3 t)-3\\sin(3 t))^2+(2\\sin(3 t)+3\\cos(3 t))^2} \\\\ &=e^{2 t}\\sqrt{4\\cos(3 t)^2-12\\cos(3 t)\\sin(3 t)+9\\sin(3 t)^2+4\\sin(3 t)^2+12\\cos(3 t)\\sin(3 t)+9\\cos(3 t)^2} \\\\ &=e^{2 t}\\sqrt{13(\\cos^2(3 t)+\\sin^2(3 t))} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{13} e^{2 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{13} e^{2 t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\sqrt{13} \\int_{1}^{2}e^{2 t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{13} e^{2 t}}{2}\\big|_{1}^{2} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}\\left(e^{4}-e^{2}\\right) \\\\ &=- \\frac{\\sqrt{13} \\left(1 - e^{2}\\right) e^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534188 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0766a4f7-f52f-5043-ae35-a856b4a3b23e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{56}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534179} {:answer/id #uuid "5421a2be-ff41-52b4-9e3a-33ab45fb9720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534190} {:answer/id #uuid "8535033e-8b75-5a23-8e58-54e25185cffa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{42704}{405}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534194} {:answer/id #uuid "c4faa60e-300e-587b-9890-74b781dea4b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{28}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534202} {:answer/id #uuid "fea636fd-e27c-58c7-8f64-44b0aeb12645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4faa60e-300e-587b-9890-74b781dea4b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{28}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534202} :answer-field/id #uuid "13577cdf-f8b5-5512-884e-ecd8f2676e0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4a67251d-20e1-510a-85b5-4eba157c1a4f" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $$\n\\displaystyle r(t)=\\langle 4 t + 2,- \\frac{\\left(2 t + 1\\right)^{3}}{3} - \\frac{1}{2 t + 1}\\rangle\n$$ from $t=0$ to $t=1$.\n\n![](images/8d/8d83a591169c9ac41f6637a985554b0b907fa017349bf92c9197618a3f61409b.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t)&=\\left\\langle\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(4 t + 2),\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(- \\frac{\\left(2 t + 1\\right)^{3}}{3} - \\frac{1}{2 t + 1})\\right\\rangle \\\\ &=\\left\\langle 4,- 2 \\left(2 t + 1\\right)^{2} + \\frac{2}{\\left(2 t + 1\\right)^{2}}\\right\\rangle \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(4)^2+(- 2 \\left(2 t + 1\\right)^{2} + \\frac{2}{\\left(2 t + 1\\right)^{2}})^2} \\\\ &=2\\sqrt{4+\\left(\\frac{1}{(2 t + 1)^2}-(2 t + 1)^2\\right)^2} \\\\ &=2\\sqrt{4+\\frac{1}{(2 t + 1)^4}-2+(2 t + 1)^4} \\\\ &=2\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{(2 t + 1)^4}+2+(2 t + 1)^4} \\\\ &=2\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1}{(2 t + 1)^2}+(2 t + 1)^2\\right)^2} \\\\ &=2 \\left(2 t + 1\\right)^{2} + \\frac{2}{\\left(2 t + 1\\right)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $2 t + 1>0$ throughout the given interval.\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=2 t + 1$, $\\mathrm{d}u=2\\mathrm{d}t$.\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{0}^{1}2 \\left(2 t + 1\\right)^{2} + \\frac{2}{\\left(2 t + 1\\right)^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{1}^{3}u^{2} + \\frac{1}{u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ &=\\frac{u^{3}}{3} - \\frac{1}{u}\\big|_{1}^{3} \\\\ &=1\\left[\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{3^3}{3}\\right)-\\left(-\\frac{1}{1}+\\frac{1^3}{3}\\right)\\right] \\\\ &=\\frac{28}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534191 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71124825-5a14-5d2d-a9b0-c7ad1ba3446f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\sqrt{10} \\left(1 - e^{3}\\right)}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534193} {:answer/id #uuid "9b193ff6-feec-5dc4-8426-d3a3b2e73a76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5}{3} + \\frac{5 e^{6}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534199} {:answer/id #uuid "cd4233bb-a74f-5f83-9cff-036e66ffdd63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\left(-1 + e^{3} \\cos{\\left(1 \\right)}\\right)^{2} + e^{6} \\sin^{2}{\\left(1 \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534204} {:answer/id #uuid "e3d729ff-9410-5b97-b282-4823fbd2cd10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{10} \\left(1 - e^{3}\\right)}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534206} {:answer/id #uuid "fb69b648-f5f7-5b3d-8d7d-d9a280b5aee9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\sqrt{10} \\left(1 - e^{3}\\right)}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71124825-5a14-5d2d-a9b0-c7ad1ba3446f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\sqrt{10} \\left(1 - e^{3}\\right)}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534193} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc84ff7e-5891-5dea-8949-00c1c415c6c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534203}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5ace710b-6335-5e78-8b4b-e85c65902917" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $r(t)=\\langle e^{3 t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},e^{3 t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\rangle$ from $t=0$ to $t=1$.\n\n![](images/fc/fc465a88c6e529608e8a366c1822b0f8b6e3bde20e30233f25c4a2708369d06f.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t)&=\\left\\langle\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(e^{3 t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}),\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(e^{3 t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\right\\rangle \\\\ &=\\left\\langle - e^{3 t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 3 e^{3 t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},3 e^{3 t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + e^{3 t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right\\rangle \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(- e^{3 t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 3 e^{3 t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2+(3 e^{3 t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + e^{3 t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2} \\\\ &=e^{3 t}\\sqrt{(3\\cos(t)-1\\sin(t))^2+(3\\sin(t)+1\\cos(t))^2} \\\\ &=e^{3 t}\\sqrt{9\\cos(t)^2-6\\cos(t)\\sin(t)+1\\sin(t)^2+9\\sin(t)^2+6\\cos(t)\\sin(t)+1\\cos(t)^2} \\\\ &=e^{3 t}\\sqrt{10(\\cos^2(t)+\\sin^2(t))} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{10} e^{3 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{10} e^{3 t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\sqrt{10} \\int_{0}^{1}e^{3 t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{10} e^{3 t}}{3}\\big|_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{3}\\left(e^{3}-1\\right) \\\\ &=- \\frac{\\sqrt{10} \\left(1 - e^{3}\\right)}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534196 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13952e9a-df42-5290-b84a-bc75ebfffe42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\sqrt{5} \\left(1 - e^{2}\\right)}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534182} {:answer/id #uuid "4f0a2b8f-d15c-59ef-83a6-d509a32e7e08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\sqrt{5} \\left(1 - e^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534189} {:answer/id #uuid "6e666bec-d6c4-5297-8aad-fa9656539027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{5}{4} + \\frac{5 e^{4}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534192} {:answer/id #uuid "bcbfe11c-5b05-5ddf-b041-31ede0d8c6ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\left(-1 + e^{2} \\cos{\\left(1 \\right)}\\right)^{2} + e^{4} \\sin^{2}{\\left(1 \\right)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534201} {:answer/id #uuid "feff593c-5dbc-51e6-bb47-daac0931cbc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\sqrt{5} \\left(1 - e^{2}\\right)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "feff593c-5dbc-51e6-bb47-daac0931cbc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{\\sqrt{5} \\left(1 - e^{2}\\right)}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534212} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbbc8536-bf3a-503b-97a6-fe1f8c659659" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534200}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "918b2263-6a41-5532-8840-aa9f0d567ce6" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $r(t)=\\langle e^{2 t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},e^{2 t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\rangle$ from $t=0$ to $t=1$.\n\n![](images/68/68033bf43d06f91b46c76c7cc02021269035a64fe610a9513efc847219fbc2dc.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t)&=\\left\\langle\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(e^{2 t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}),\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(e^{2 t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\right\\rangle \\\\ &=\\left\\langle - e^{2 t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 e^{2 t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)},2 e^{2 t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + e^{2 t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right\\rangle \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(- e^{2 t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 e^{2 t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2+(2 e^{2 t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + e^{2 t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})^2} \\\\ &=e^{2 t}\\sqrt{(2\\cos(t)-1\\sin(t))^2+(2\\sin(t)+1\\cos(t))^2} \\\\ &=e^{2 t}\\sqrt{4\\cos(t)^2-4\\cos(t)\\sin(t)+1\\sin(t)^2+4\\sin(t)^2+4\\cos(t)\\sin(t)+1\\cos(t)^2} \\\\ &=e^{2 t}\\sqrt{5(\\cos^2(t)+\\sin^2(t))} \\\\ &=\\sqrt{5} e^{2 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{5} e^{2 t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\sqrt{5} \\int_{0}^{1}e^{2 t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{5} e^{2 t}}{2}\\big|_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\left(e^{2}-1\\right) \\\\ &=- \\frac{\\sqrt{5} \\left(1 - e^{2}\\right)}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
